in a particular crop at any given moment **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to **the number of bacteria** at that moment..* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of bacteria* in a particular crop varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of bacteria* at the moment. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}∝B.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of bacteria *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-kB.\n$$" 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281810 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281811 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281812 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281813 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281814 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1041 "selection" 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281811 13194139534197 true] [17592186281809 1110 #uuid "99d16e8d-cf11-5676-87a1-e8b7d6cc7fb5" 13194139534197 true] [17592186281810 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{B},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534197 true] [17592186281810 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534197 true] [17592186281810 1111 #uuid "51f8e7f5-b543-5151-b6a5-e1edb10f17f1" 13194139534197 true] [17592186281811 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-kB,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534197 true] [17592186281811 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534197 true] [17592186281811 1111 #uuid "a7f47d35-0b83-5c74-b3b4-3ba60752e64f" 1